Nearly all configurations of the Apple Watch SE 3 are suddenly "unavailable" on Apple's online store in the U.S. and other countries we checked, for reasons unknown.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2025/09/Apple-Watch-SE-3-1.jpg" alt="" width="2510" height="1412" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1019914" /><br/>
Apple is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/26/apple-iphone-event-2026/">holding an event this Wednesday</a> to announce new iPhones and Apple Watches, but an Apple Watch SE 4 was not expected tomorrow, as new generations of the Apple Watch SE have never been released in back-to-back years. The original Apple Watch SE debuted in September 2020, the Apple Watch SE 2 arrived in September 2022, and the Apple Watch SE 3 was announced in September 2025.<br/>
<br/>
Is this a sign that an Apple Watch SE 4 will be announced tomorrow after all, or is this simply a temporary issue that will be resolved soon? We shall see.<br/>
